.TH LPARSER 1 "2026-05" "BusyPipe 1.0" "BusyPipe Manual"
.SH NAME
lparser \- structured log parser for BusyPipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lparser
[\fB\-\-regex\fR \fIPATTERN\fR \fB\-\-fields\fR \fIf1,f2,...\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-csv\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-stats\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lparser
reads raw log lines from standard input, extracts named fields using POSIX
extended regular expressions (capture groups), and writes structured
\fBCSV\fR or \fBJSONL\fR output to standard output.

It is the first stage of the BusyPipe ETL pipeline:

.nf
  lparser | lfilter | lstore
.fi

Lines that do not match the pattern are silently skipped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-regex " " \fIPATTERN\fR
POSIX extended regular expression.  Each capture group corresponds to one
output field.
.TP
.BR \-\-fields " " \fIf1,f2,...\fR
Comma-separated list of field names.  The count must match the number of
capture groups in \fI\-\-regex\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fINAME\fR
Use a built-in format (see \fBBUILT-IN FORMATS\fR below).
Implies both \fI\-\-regex\fR and \fI\-\-fields\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-csv
Write output as CSV.  The first line is the header. (default)
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Write output as JSONL: one JSON object per matched line.
.TP
.BR \-\-stats
Print \fImatched=N skipped=N total=N\fR to stderr after processing.
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.SH BUILT-IN FORMATS
.TP
.B nginx
Nginx / Apache Combined Access Log.
Fields: \fBip,time,method,path,status,bytes\fR
.TP
.B apache
Apache Common Log Format.
Fields: \fBip,time,method,path,status,bytes\fR
.TP
.B auth
SSH \fIauth.log\fR (\fIsshd\fR Failed/Accepted password events).
Fields: \fBtime,host,result,user,src_ip,port\fR
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, invalid regex, or other runtime error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Parse Nginx access log (CSV)
.nf
  lparser \-\-format nginx \-\-csv < /var/log/nginx/access.log
.fi
.SS Parse auth.log (JSONL)
.nf
  lparser \-\-format auth \-\-json < /var/log/auth.log
.fi
.SS Custom regex
.nf
  lparser \-\-regex '^([0-9.]+) .* "([A-Z]+) ([^ ]+)' \\
          \-\-fields ip,method,path \-\-csv < access.log
.fi
.SS Full pipeline
.nf
  lparser \-\-format nginx \-\-csv < access.log \\
    | lfilter \-\-where 'status>=400' \-\-select 'ip,path,status' \\
    | lstore  \-\-db errors.tsv \-\-put \-\-key\-field ip \-\-ttl 3600
.fi
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Implements a subset of \fBawk\fR(1) / \fBgrep\fR(1) functionality optimised for
structured log parsing.  The CSV output is compatible with GNU \fBcut\fR(1) and
standard CSV processors.
.SH BUGS
Quoted CSV fields are not yet supported.
Lines longer than 4096 bytes are truncated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfilter (1),
.BR lstore (1),
.BR grep (1),
.BR awk (1),
.BR regex (7)
